":"ca-chaptered","code":null,"date":"2026-08-20","eventType":"chaptered","historyId":"118936164","location":"Secretary of State","sequence":18,"significance":"major","source":null,"status":null,"text":"Chaptered by Secretary of State. Chapter 115, Statutes of 2026.","time":null,"votes":[]}],"affectedStatutes":[{"action":"IS_AMENDED","code":"EDC","text":"Section 5322 of the Education Code is amended to read:"},{"action":"IS_AMENDED","code":"ELEC","text":"Section 12283 of the Elections Code is amended to read:"}],"approvedDate":"2026-08-20","chapter":{"citation":"Chapter 115, Statutes of 2026","number":"115","type":"CHP","year":"2026"},"chapteredDate":"2026-08-20","committees":[],"conditions":[],"contentHash":"2ca83e868734ea70e6bba230a8524901a52b5b426f0f2da3f7c1917ca058a088","cosponsorCount":null,"digest":"When an election for governing board members of a school district or community college district is ordered, existing law requires the governing board of the district, or the board or officer authorized by law to make such designations, to adopt a resolution specifying the date and the purpose of the election and requires that resolution to be delivered, not fewer than 123 days before the election, to the county superintendent of schools and the officer conducting the election, as provided.\n\nThis bill would require that resolution to instead be delivered not fewer than 125 days before the election.\n\nExisting law authorizes the governing body with jurisdiction over school buildings or other public buildings to allow its buildings to be used for polling places, for vote centers beginning up to 10 days before the election, or to store voting machines and other vote-tabulating devices. On the day that a school building is used as a polling place or vote center, the governing body may continue school in session, designate the day for staff training and development, or close the school.\n\nThis bill would require the governing body to continue school in session on any schoolday when a school building is used for a vote center, except on election day when the governing body may continue school in session, designate the day for staff training and development, or close the school.\n\nThe bill would make related clarifying and conforming changes.","digestDate":null,"digestVersion":null,"effective":{"basis":"not_verified","date":null,"note":"No effective date is recorded in the official bill data and DemocracyHQ has not verified one. A non-urgency statute enacted in a regular session generally takes effect on January 1 after a 90-day period (Cal. Const. art. IV, § 8(c)), but a bill may state other operative dates."},"expiryClauses":[],"firstObservedAt":"2026-11-20T01:12:59Z","id":"ca-20252026-sb1430","identifier":"SB 1430","indicators":{"Appropriation":"NO","BudgetBill":"NO","Election":"NO","FiscalCommittee":"NO","ImmediateEffect":"NO","LocalProgram":"NO","TaxLevy":"NO","Urgency":"NO","UsualCurrentExpenses":"NO","VoteRequired":"MAJORITY"},"introducedDate":"2026-03-05","issueTags":[{"matchCount":null,"matchedField":"Legislative Counsel's digest","matchedText":"buildings to allow its buildings to be used for polling places, for vote centers beginning up to 10 days","ruleId":"tag-admin-2","tag":"election-administration"},{"matchCount":null,"matchedField":"Legislative Counsel's digest","matchedText":"10 days before the election, or to store voting machines and other vote-tabulating devices. On the","ruleId":"tag-tech-1","tag":"voting-technology"}],"judicialNote":"Legislative status does not show whether a court has blocked, narrowed or upheld any provision. Check the linked litigation, which may be incomplete.","lastActionDate":"2026-08-20","lastActionText":"Chaptered by Secretary of State. Chapter 115, Statutes of 2026.","lastCheckedAt":"2026-11-21T14:35:54Z","leadAuthors":"Introduced by Committee on Elections and Constitutional Amendments (Senators Wiener (Chair), Allen, Cervantes, Choi, and Umberg)","legislativeStatus":{"currentHouse":